# Rank 1802 / CVE-2024-53677 (CWE-22, CWE-20): a Struts 2.3.x file upload
# publishes the interceptor's own parameter names -- <inputName>,
# <inputName>ContentType, <inputName>FileName -- into the request's
# parameter map, over entries an attacker has supplied as extra
# multipart form fields. The remediation for the earlier traversal over
# these names removed an existing entry before the put only when its key
# is case-insensitively equal to the interceptor's key:
#
#   private void putCaseInsensitive(Map<String, Object> params, String key, Object value) {
#       Iterator<Map.Entry<String, Object>> iterator = params.entrySet().iterator();
#       while (iterator.hasNext()) {
#           Map.Entry<String, Object> entry = iterator.next();
#           if (key.equalsIgnoreCase(entry.getKey())) {
#               iterator.remove();
#           }
#       }
#       params.put(key, value);
#   }
#
# The parameters binder downstream evaluates every surviving key as an
# OGNL expression, and `top.uploadFileName[0]` -- a key that contains
# the published name without being equal to it -- survives the
# equality-only removal, navigates onto the action's uploadFileName
# property, and hands the attacker the stored file name: path traversal
# through a parameter the library thought it had overridden. The fixed revision
# (930fef76, "Extend check before adding file upload params") widens
# the removal predicate from equality to containment:
#
#   if (entry.getKey().toLowerCase().contains(key.toLowerCase())) {
#
# and, because containment on the bare inputName would delete unrelated
# parameters, reverts that one put to a plain params.put -- the derived
# ContentType/FileName names keep the checked put.
#
# What fires without this change. `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off
# --max-ram 6GB` over core/src/main/java/org/apache/struts2/interceptor
# reports 7 findings at 056228cd (the fixed revision's parent) and the same 7 at
# 930fef76, three --cache off runs each, none of them in
# FileUploadInterceptor.java; over core/src/main/java both revisions
# report 49 findings, identical sets. `vyql match` on the file labels
# only getLocaleProvider.getLocale as code.HttpInput and an unrelated
# HtmlRender arg; `vyql graph` shows the vulnerable helper fully
# lowered -- key.equalsIgnoreCase (Call), iterator.remove (Call),
# params.put (Call), with the params and key params flowing into them
# -- so the engine resolves everything and no construct is mishandled.
# Findings elsewhere in the tree are not coverage.
#
# No binding is shippable here, and the reason is structural. The fixed revision
# changes one string-comparison predicate inside a private helper; the
# dataflow at both revisions is identical (the request's parameter map
# in, the same put out), so no taint route can separate them and no
# API-documented call left inside the guarded method differs between
# revisions -- the guarded-method counterweight does not apply. The
# only available discriminators are the fixed revision's own vocabulary: the
# helper names (putCaseInsensitive / putWithCheck), or the removal
# predicate's spelling. Keying the neutraliser on `contains` fires on
# four equally-enforcing variants of the patched form (indexOf(key) >=
# 0, a regionMatches scan, Pattern.quote(key) with find, startsWith/
# endsWith pairs) and keys the binding to the incident rather than the
# weakness. Keying the finding on equality-only removal -- flag
# equalsIgnoreCase guarding an entry removal before a map put -- puts
# the judgement in the binding layer, and the judgement is only true
# where an expression-evaluating binder consumes the map: the same
# equality removal over a config or session map is correct code, and
# the consumer is invisible at the removal site. Enumerated rather
# than sampled, the loose form (equalsIgnoreCase plus a remove plus a
# put in one 40-line window) matches 16 files across every repository
# cloned for this campaign (130,080 Java files), 15 besides this one;
# the tight single-function form matches 3 -- a NiFi session
# scheduler, an OpenAM attribute mapper, a Snowflake JDBC addBatch --
# all ordinary equality-keyed maps where the removal is sound. The
# name-worthy weakness class (parameter override with incomplete
# removal) has no concept, and minting one that fires only where an
# expression binder consumes the map is this incident's shape, not a
# class unrelated code can hit. This sits with the measured family of
# fixes that strengthen an existing control's completeness -- the
# 1500-1616 wiring/configuration rows and the rejection of
# discriminators encoding the fixing commit's own layout. No
# ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: the graph resolves the whole helper. No
# definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1802 records the
# equality-only override, the patched containment form, and an
# equality removal over a plain map, all asserting reject
# VYQL-PATH-001: when parameter-override vocabulary lands, the
# equality-only override form must flip to expect.

test "rank1802: upload parameter names published into the request parameter map after an equality-only removal"
  lang java
  file FileUploadInterceptor.java
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  import java.util.ArrayList;
  import java.util.Iterator;
  import java.util.List;
  import java.util.Map;

  public class FileUploadInterceptor {

      public String intercept(MultiPartRequestWrapper multiWrapper, ActionContext ac) {
          Enumeration fileParameterNames = multiWrapper.getFileParameterNames();
          while (fileParameterNames.hasMoreElements()) {
              String inputName = (String) fileParameterNames.nextElement();
              String[] fileName = multiWrapper.getFileNames(inputName);
              File[] files = multiWrapper.getFiles(inputName);
              if (files != null && files.length > 0) {
                  List<File> acceptedFiles = new ArrayList<File>(files.length);
                  List<String> acceptedFileNames = new ArrayList<String>(files.length);
                  for (int index = 0; index < files.length; index++) {
                      acceptedFiles.add(files[index]);
                      acceptedFileNames.add(fileName[index]);
                  }
                  if (!acceptedFiles.isEmpty()) {
                      Map<String, Object> params = ac.getParameters();
                      String fileNameName = inputName + "FileName";
                      putCaseInsensitive(params, inputName, acceptedFiles.toArray(new File[acceptedFiles.size()]));
                      putCaseInsensitive(params, fileNameName, acceptedFileNames.toArray(new String[acceptedFileNames.size()]));
                  }
              }
          }
          return "success";
      }

      private void putCaseInsensitive(Map<String, Object> params, String key, Object value) {
          Iterator<Map.Entry<String, Object>> iterator = params.entrySet().iterator();
          while (iterator.hasNext()) {
              Map.Entry<String, Object> entry = iterator.next();
              if (key.equalsIgnoreCase(entry.getKey())) {
                  iterator.remove();
              }
          }
          params.put(key, value);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1802: containment removal drops the embedding keys before the parameter put"
  lang java
  file FileUploadInterceptorPatched.java
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  import java.util.ArrayList;
  import java.util.Iterator;
  import java.util.List;
  import java.util.Map;

  public class FileUploadInterceptorPatched {

      public String intercept(MultiPartRequestWrapper multiWrapper, ActionContext ac) {
          Enumeration fileParameterNames = multiWrapper.getFileParameterNames();
          while (fileParameterNames.hasMoreElements()) {
              String inputName = (String) fileParameterNames.nextElement();
              String[] fileName = multiWrapper.getFileNames(inputName);
              File[] files = multiWrapper.getFiles(inputName);
              if (files != null && files.length > 0) {
                  List<File> acceptedFiles = new ArrayList<File>(files.length);
                  List<String> acceptedFileNames = new ArrayList<String>(files.length);
                  for (int index = 0; index < files.length; index++) {
                      acceptedFiles.add(files[index]);
                      acceptedFileNames.add(fileName[index]);
                  }
                  if (!acceptedFiles.isEmpty()) {
                      Map<String, Object> params = ac.getParameters();
                      String fileNameName = inputName + "FileName";
                      params.put(inputName, acceptedFiles.toArray(new File[acceptedFiles.size()]));
                      putWithCheck(params, fileNameName, acceptedFileNames.toArray(new String[acceptedFileNames.size()]));
                  }
              }
          }
          return "success";
      }

      private void putWithCheck(Map<String, Object> params, String key, Object value) {
          Iterator<Map.Entry<String, Object>> iterator = params.entrySet().iterator();
          while (iterator.hasNext()) {
              Map.Entry<String, Object> entry = iterator.next();
              if (entry.getKey().toLowerCase().contains(key.toLowerCase())) {
                  iterator.remove();
              }
          }
          params.put(key, value);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1802: equality removal over a map no expression binder consumes is correct code"
  lang java
  file ScopeMapOverride.java
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  import java.util.Iterator;
  import java.util.Map;

  public class ScopeMapOverride {

      public void registerScope(Map<String, Object> scopes, String scopeName, Object handler) {
          Iterator<Map.Entry<String, Object>> iterator = scopes.entrySet().iterator();
          while (iterator.hasNext()) {
              Map.Entry<String, Object> entry = iterator.next();
              if (scopeName.equalsIgnoreCase(entry.getKey())) {
                  iterator.remove();
              }
          }
          scopes.put(scopeName, handler);
      }
  }
  ```
